# ErgoWorks Consulting Campaign Plan

## 1. Executive summary

ErgoWorks Consulting already has a mature Google Search program. This plan is an optimisation and expansion programme—not a greenfield launch.

The recommended strategy is to:

1. **Protect and improve existing Search demand capture** by cleaning conversion goals, auditing query quality, strengthening Brand coverage and routing paid traffic to relevant landing-page variants.
2. **Open Meta as the missing demand-generation lever** using workplace- and role-level creative, beginning with one consolidated prospecting ad set.
3. **Launch a dedicated conversion landing page** centred on the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot—**preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis**.
4. **Connect media to qualified pipeline outcomes** through CRM stages, offline conversion imports, server-side tagging and Meta CAPI.
5. **Keep PMax and paid remarketing parked unless their funding, measurement, privacy and isolation gates can be met.**

The preferred minimum launch envelope is **A$4,846 per 30-day planning period**: preserve the verified A$4,246 last-30-day Search baseline and add A$600 for one Meta prospecting ad set. This remains subject to commercial approval, Snapshot delivery capacity, landing-page readiness and the Australian privacy gate.

No target CPA, kill decision or scale commitment is defensible until conversion pollution is removed and average contract value, delivery margin and qualified-lead outcomes are known.

## 2. The big idea

### See the risk. Act on the priorities. Prove implementation.

ErgoWorks should sell a practical implementation path rather than an isolated assessment:

| Strategic layer | Role |
|---|---|
| Optimise existing Search | Capture established commercial demand more accurately and efficiently |
| Add Meta demand generation | Reach WHS/HSE, HR/People & Culture, Facilities and Operations buyers before they search |
| Introduce the Snapshot | Give cold prospects a defined, low-commitment first step |
| Use a dedicated landing page | Replace generic WordPress destinations with message-matched conversion journeys |
| Fix measurement | Optimise toward qualified Consulting opportunities rather than newsletters and soft actions |
| Evaluate PMax and remarketing | Activate only when properly funded, isolated and measurable |

Search remains the proven demand-capture engine. Meta adds the top-of-funnel reach that the current programme lacks. The landing page and Snapshot connect those channels to a coherent commercial journey, while the measurement rebuild ensures future allocation is based on qualified pipeline rather than raw platform conversions.

## 3. Current-state snapshot

### Verified account baseline

| Item | Verified position |
|---|---|
| Google Ads account | **9258098368** |
| GA4 property | **316175981** |
| Focus campaign | **700072710 — Ergoworks Consulting Search** |
| Bidding | **Maximize Conversions**, no target CPA, standard strategy with no portfolio |
| Existing foundations | Auto-tagging on; GA4-linked conversions |
| Search investment | Approximately **A$40,000 trailing 12 months** |
| Observed monthly range | Approximately **A$3.0k–A$4.7k per month** |
| Last 30 days | **A$4,246 spend; 4,540 impressions; 407 clicks; 26 reported conversions** |
| Estimated real leads | Approximately **20 in the last 30 days** |
| Indicative real-lead cost | Approximately **A$212 per lead** |
| Paid social | **Zero paid-social activity in GA4 over the last 90 days** |
| PMax | Campaign 16143562968 paused |
| Display remarketing | Campaign 843760968 paused |

The 26 reported last-30-day conversions include:

- 10 Calls from ads
- 10 Make an Enquiry conversions
- 4 Newsletter Sign Ups counted as Primary
- 1 Email Click
- 1 Call Forwarding

This means reported conversion volume overstates genuine leads and currently gives Maximize Conversions an impure optimisation signal. There is no qualified-lead or closed-won import.

### Search concentration

Manual Handling Training received **A$2,069—49% of the A$4,246 last-30-day spend**. Manual handling training remains the current spend anchor and largest verified **TRAINING** term at **2,700 Australian searches per month**; research also identifies an approximately **3,400-searches-per-month mixed-intent certificate/course pool** with buyer type **UNCLASSIFIED** and an approximately **780-searches-per-month care-sector opportunity**. These are directional demand estimates, not forecasts or verified service fit, and both expansion pockets remain gated as set out in Appendices A–D.

Other notable last-30-day results include:

| Ad group | Spend | Reported conversions | Interpretation |
|---|---:|---:|---|
| Manual Handling Training | A$2,069 | 10.5 | Dominant demand, but query and lead quality are unverified |
| “DSA — Ergoworks Consulting” | A$795 | 4.5 | Not DSA: nine static EXACT terms form a competitor/generic group; total quality is unverified, while only the sampled government/competitor-query subset was near-zero converting |
| Ergonomic Office Consulting | A$719 | 7 | Reported CPA approximately A$103; validate conversion quality before expansion |
| Ergonomics Assessments | A$531 | 3 | Diagnose after conversion cleanup |
| Workplace Ergonomics | A$133 | 1 | Insufficient evidence for a directional decision |
| Brand | A$0 | 0 | All three dedicated Brand terms are paused; the same three terms are duplicated across five service groups, so repair requires in-place re-enablement and de-duplication before any breakout decision |

Paid traffic currently lands on generic WordPress pages, led by the Manual Handling Training page with 234 clicks in the last 30 days. There is no dedicated paid-media conversion page.

### Scope limitation

The available evidence includes last-30-day search terms, the full keyword inventory with match types, statuses and headline Quality Scores, 493 negatives and a partial geography signal. Remaining gaps are longer search-term and keyword-performance history, the negative-list audit, RSAs/assets, complete campaign settings, Quality Score components and geo/device performance reports. Consequently, the package supports a diagnostic plan—not unconditional pause, restructure or scale instructions.

The shared Ads account also contains Physiotherapy activity. Consulting goals, tags, audiences and campaign controls must be isolated without applying account-wide negatives or exclusions that could damage Physiotherapy.

## 4. Offer and positioning

### Core position

ErgoWorks should be positioned as the workplace-ergonomics implementation partner that helps organisations:

- establish visibility over workplace-ergonomics priorities;
- translate findings into practical actions and responsibilities;
- create repeatable implementation and reporting evidence.

The promise is controllable outputs—not guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance, claims reductions or medical outcomes.

### Canonical offer registry — client approval required before launch

| Stage | Offer | Eligibility / best fit | Exact deliverable and pricing status | Required caveat |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Entry | **Free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot** | B2B organisational buyer with one defined workplace-ergonomics question; capacity and service geography must be approved | 15-minute consultant conversation and written three-point summary; free, subject to approved fulfilment capacity | Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis |
| Paid entry | **ErgoStart** | Defined site, cohort or issue | Fixed-scope assessment sprint and prioritised actions; pricing unconfirmed and must not be advertised until client-approved | Scope, inclusions, delivery timing and price are confirmed only in an approved proposal |
| Rollout | **ErgoScale** | Corporate, multi-site or hybrid programme | Repeatable workflow, implementation plan and reporting; pricing unconfirmed | Coverage, timing and outputs depend on the approved programme scope |
| Capability | **ErgoCoach** | Manual-task or train-the-trainer need | Task-led review, tailored training and supervisor toolkit; pricing unconfirmed | Format, participants and outputs depend on the approved scope |
| Ongoing | **ErgoControl** | Organisation requiring ongoing programme visibility | ErgoAssess subscription or managed retainer, review cadence and reporting; pricing unconfirmed | Platform, service level, cadence and outputs depend on the approved scope |

The Snapshot gives cold prospects a concrete next step without asking them to commit immediately to a full programme. The offer names, eligibility, fulfilment promise and ladder remain **client sign-off required**.

Detailed positioning and creative direction are in [Appendix D](./appendices/D-creative-briefs.md).

## 5. Channel and budget at a glance

All budgets use a **30-day planning period**. They are anchored to both the approximately **A$40,000 trailing-12-month Search investment** and the observed **A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range**, with the verified **A$4,246 last-30-day spend** as the exact planning baseline.

| Scenario | Search | Meta | PMax | Remarketing | Total | Recommendation |
|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|---|
| **1. Flat-budget reallocation** | A$3,646 | A$600 | A$0 | A$0 | **A$4,246** | Use only if total media must remain flat |
| **2. Minimum Meta on top** | A$4,246 | A$600 | A$0 | A$0 | **A$4,846** | **Preferred minimum launch scenario** |
| **3. Meta plus funded PMax** | A$4,246 | A$600 | A$1,500 | A$0 | **A$6,346** | Consider only after all PMax gates pass |

### Platform floors

| Channel | Planning floor | Implication |
|---|---:|---|
| Meta | **A$20/day or A$600 per ad set per 30 days** | Keep the initial budget in one consolidated prospecting ad set |
| PMax | **A$50/day or A$1,500 per 30 days** | A nominal 5–10% allocation is not viable at the current run-rate |
| Paid remarketing | Separate viable budget plus sufficient audience size | Build audiences first; park paid delivery initially |

The provisional Meta Snapshot-request CPA planning range of **A$53.08–A$84.92** is assumption-based, not observed performance or a commercial target. It assumes the lower-friction Snapshot request costs 25%–40% of the current approximately A$212 raw Search lead cost. It must be replaced with observed data.

PMax should be **funded to its floor or parked**. Across the observed A$3.0k–A$4.7k monthly range, its floor would consume approximately 31.9%–50.0% of the budget. Paid remarketing should not share PMax’s A$1,500 testing allocation.

Detailed channel structure, keywords, floors and conditional decision tables are in [Appendix B](./appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md). The existing-account diagnostic is in [Appendix E](./appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md).

## 6. Landing-page concept

Build one dedicated, navigation-reduced landing-page system on an approved ErgoWorks Consulting destination.

### Page principles

- **Launch default:** one dominant CTA on every baseline variant: request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot—preliminary guidance only, **not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis**. Service-plan-primary variants are post-baseline tests only.
- Message-matched variants led by:

  1. Manual Handling Training
  2. Workstation and Ergonomic Assessment
  3. Hybrid and Home-office programmes

- Stripped header with ErgoWorks identity, an optional phone contact and no store or Physiotherapy navigation.
- Two-step form:

  1. business contact details;
  2. non-sensitive qualification fields such as team-size band, service need, location and timeframe.

- No injury history, symptoms, diagnoses, treatment, claim details or other health information.
- Separate required enquiry consent from optional, unchecked marketing consent.
- Clear explanation of what the Snapshot includes, what happens next and what it does not represent.
- Mobile-first performance, source/click-ID capture and a clear thank-you journey.
- Proof only after substantiation and written client approval.

The complete page architecture and copy are in [Appendix A](./appendices/A-landing-page-copy.md).

## 7. Measurement approach

Measurement is an upgrade to existing GA4-linked tracking—not a rebuild from zero.

### Conversion hierarchy

| Stage | Treatment |
|---|---|
| Valid Consulting enquiry | Primary initially |
| Qualified new-business Consulting call | Primary only when qualification rules can be enforced or reconciled |
| Valid B2B Snapshot request | Primary initially; preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis |
| CRM-qualified lead | Primary offline import once reliable |
| Proposal and closed-won | Downstream/value signals as volume and data quality permit |
| Newsletter, email click, click-to-call, call forwarding and local actions | Secondary |
| Physiotherapy actions | Excluded from Consulting campaign goals |

### Measurement stack

- Preserve Google auto-tagging and the existing GA4 link.
- Use campaign-specific Consulting conversion goals.
- Capture GCLID, GBRAID, WBRAID, FBCLID and UTMs in the CRM.
- Send qualified-lead, proposal and closed-won outcomes through Google Data Manager and Meta CAPI.
- Implement server-side GTM on a first-party domain such as `tags.ergoworksconsulting.com.au`.
- Use a Conversion Linker and Meta Pixel plus CAPI, preferably through CAPI Gateway.
- Use matching browser/server `event_id` values for deduplication.
- Use Data-Driven Attribution where eligible; do not use rule-based attribution.
- Implement **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, through an approved CMP.
- Enforce no pre-consent advertising or analytics transmissions unless Australian privacy/legal review explicitly approves a different configuration.
- Keep Consulting separate from Physiotherapy, ErgoEquip and Biosymm through dedicated or tightly scoped GA4 stream, Meta Dataset/Pixel, GTM triggers, audiences and CRM mappings.

### First-90-day measurement commitments

- 100% of approved Primary actions documented and tested.
- Newsletter and soft actions removed from Consulting bidding goals.
- Physiotherapy actions excluded from campaign 700072710 goals.
- CRM lead IDs and event IDs captured on valid lead records.
- Offline-event latency below 24 hours where operationally possible; 24–72 hours is a warning range.
- Meta lead-event EMQ of at least 8.0.
- Browser/server deduplication of at least 90%.
- Server/client hit ratio between 80% and 120%.
- At least six applicable Meta match parameters on eligible events.
- Weekly platform-to-CRM reconciliation.
- Zero sensitive-data events or parameters detected in testing.

The primary commercial KPI is **cost per qualified lead (CPQL)**. Raw CPL remains an entry-stage diagnostic. CAC and target CPQL cannot be set until contract value, contribution margin and stage-conversion rates are verified.

The full event taxonomy, consent requirements, field allowlist/deny list and QA plan are in [Appendix C](./appendices/C-tracking-spec.md).

### Methodology conflict

The generic ads-budget rubric recommends Maximize Clicks below 30 conversions per month. The live campaign, however, is mature, already uses Maximize Conversions and generates approximately 20 real leads per month while its current conversion signal is polluted.

Automatically switching to Maximize Clicks during measurement repair could optimise for traffic volume before query quality is understood. The account-specific recommendation is therefore to retain Maximize Conversions while cleaning and restabilising the baseline, then reassess:

| Clean post-remediation condition | Bidding decision |
|---|---|
| Fewer than 20 clean conversions/month with weak delivery and no qualified-lead imports | Consider a controlled Maximize Clicks test only after query review and with an evidence-based CPC cap |
| Approximately 20–29 clean conversions/month with stable query and lead quality | Retain Maximize Conversions and document the rubric variance |
| At least 30 clean conversions/month with stable CPA | Maximize Conversions is supported; assess tCPA readiness |
| More than 50 clean conversions/month with stable qualified-lead CPA | Consider tCPA |
| Reliable margin values and sufficient closed-won volume | Assess tROAS |

Do not use ECPC.

## 8. 30/60/90 roadmap

### Days 1–30 — Establish the foundation

- Inventory all 16 enabled conversion actions and assign each to Consulting, Physiotherapy or another scope.
- Create the approved Consulting conversion-goal hierarchy.
- Demote newsletters and soft actions; exclude Physiotherapy actions from Consulting goals.
- Confirm CRM, click-ID capture, call qualification and offline-upload design.
- Complete Australian privacy/legal review, CMP and consent design.
- Build and QA the dedicated landing-page variants and two-step form.
- Extend the resolved Search evidence with longer-history query and keyword-performance pulls; audit the 493 negatives; pull RSAs, assets, settings, Quality Score components and geo/device reports.
- Repair the existing Brand ad group, remove all three confirmed duplicates from the five service groups, and verify routing and separated metrics before considering breakout.
- Prepare one isolated Meta prospecting build but keep it unpublished.
- Keep PMax and paid remarketing parked.

**Committed leading indicators:** approved goal map; zero newsletter primaries; test-event reconciliation; privacy approval; LP/form QA passed; at least 30 days of search terms reviewed.

### Days 31–60 — Launch controlled tests

- Route approved Search themes to their relevant landing-page variants.
- Retain Maximize Conversions while the clean baseline forms.
- Launch one consolidated Meta website-lead prospecting ad set under Scenario 1 or 2.
- Fund Meta at no less than A$20/day.
- Use at least three materially distinct formats and five approved creatives.
- Optimise initially to valid Snapshot requests; each Snapshot placement must state: **Preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis.**
- Validate click-ID, UTM, CRM-stage, Pixel/CAPI and deduplication flows.
- Build Consulting-only retargeting audiences without activating a separately underfunded ad set.
- Review search terms weekly and classify any product or Physiotherapy bleed.

**Committed leading indicators:** approved destination coverage; minimum Meta delivery floor; delivery, CTR, form-start and Snapshot-request baselines; identifiers retained; no known cross-business bleed left unclassified.

### Days 61–90 — Diagnose and decide

- Assign each Search cluster a status: retain, repair, insufficient data or candidate test.
- Compare Meta concepts and formats without fragmenting the budget.
- Replace the provisional Meta CPA assumption with observed Snapshot-request data.
- Reconcile raw leads to CRM-qualified leads and proposals.
- Complete the commercial target-CPA worksheet or mark it not assessable.
- Issue a written PMax fund-to-floor or park decision.
- Issue a separate paid-remarketing rebuild or park decision.
- Propose any budget increase in increments no greater than 20%, followed by 3–5 days of observation and conversion-lag review.

No segment receives an unconditional kill or scale label during the first 90 days. The 3× Kill Rule requires an approved clean target CPA, and the methodology’s full scaling threshold of at least 50 conversions per week is far above the current approximately 20 real leads per month.

Any 12-month lead, CPA or revenue trajectory remains an assumption-labelled scenario—not a commitment.

## 9. Risks and compliance gates

| Gate | Requirement | Launch consequence |
|---|---|---|
| Claims | No guaranteed injury prevention, assured WHS compliance, quantified claims reduction or guaranteed financial outcome | Blocks affected creative or page copy |
| Snapshot description | Every placement must state: preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis | Blocks affected ad, form or page |
| OAIC APP 3 | No injury, symptom, diagnosis, treatment, claim or other health fields in advertising forms | Blocks form launch |
| Meta personal attributes | Use workplace- and role-level language; never imply that the viewer or their team has a health condition | Blocks affected Meta creative |
| Consent | Required enquiry consent must be separate from optional, unchecked marketing consent | Blocks form launch |
| Privacy | Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent. CMP, pixel/CAPI field mapping, call tracking and CRM uploads require Australian privacy/legal approval | Blocks all new paid-social, LP tracking, remarketing and offline activation |
| Sensitive data | No free-text enquiry content, medical data, call content or Physiotherapy data may be sent to advertising platforms—even hashed | Blocks measurement activation |
| Proof | Awards, “ASX 100,” 5.0/63 reviews, client logos and Danone references are **client sign-off required** wherever proposed | Blocks those proof assets |
| Isolation | Campaign-level controls and Consulting-specific measurement scope must prevent ErgoEquip, Biosymm and Physiotherapy contamination | Blocks affected campaign or dataset |
| PMax | Clean goals, offline loop, dedicated LP, verified assets, URL controls, exclusions and A$50/day funding | Otherwise remains parked |
| Remarketing | Privacy approval, sufficient isolated audiences, approved creative, frequency controls and separate viable funding | Otherwise remains parked |

This document authorises planning only. It does not authorise live-account, website, CRM or tracking changes.

## 10. Open decisions

The decisions Marcus and the client need to resolve are summarised below and detailed in [Open Questions](./open-questions.md):

- Is Meta’s A$600 minimum added on top of Search or reallocated from it?
- Can PMax receive its full A$50/day floor without destabilising Search?
- What average contract value, delivery margin and close rate define the allowable CAC and target CPQL?
- Which CRM will hold click IDs, consent and lead-stage outcomes?
- How far should Consulting and Physiotherapy be separated across Ads, GA4, GTM and Meta?
- Should PMax and paid remarketing be funded properly or remain parked?
- How many Snapshot requests can the team deliver and follow up?
- Which reviews, logos, awards and client references are substantiated and approved?
- Who owns landing-page development and where will it be hosted?
- What future subdomain or route should host the private shareable campaign page?

## Not assessed / data required before implementation

| Area | Data or decision required | What it enables |
|---|---|---|
| Search queries and competitor/generic-group terms | Last 90 days plus trailing 12 months; the last-30-day pull is resolved | Longer-history query-quality diagnosis and evidence-based controls |
| Keyword and negative history | Trailing-12-month keyword performance plus audit of the resolved 493-negative inventory | Structure, routing, overblocking and overlap decisions |
| RSAs, assets and Quality Score components | Current and recent creative history; expected CTR, ad relevance and landing-page experience | Relevance, eligibility and landing-page diagnosis |
| Geography, devices and campaign settings | Geo/device performance plus location targets, presence, networks and other complete settings | Leakage, presence, device and network decisions |
| Brand post-repair evidence | Query demand, impression share, lost share and auction insights after in-place consolidation | Retain repaired ad group versus campaign breakout |
| Conversion configuration | All 16 enabled actions and campaign-specific goal mappings | Clean Consulting bidding objective |
| Call outcomes | Duration plus business-purpose dispositions | Qualified-call validation |
| CRM pipeline | Qualified, proposal, won, revenue and contribution-margin stages joined to click IDs | Target CPQL, CAC and value-bidding readiness |
| PMax history and controls | Assets, search categories, themes, URLs, exclusions, goals and historical outcomes | Fund-to-floor versus park decision |
| Remarketing configuration | Audience sources, size, duration, exclusions, frequency and history | Rebuild versus park decision |
| Privacy and consent | CMP, collection notices, vendor flows, retention and legal approval | Pre-launch approval |
| Proof permissions | Substantiation and written approval for reviews, logos, awards, Danone and “ASX 100” | Paid-media proof usage |
| Commercial economics | Average contract value, delivery margin, close rates and acceptable payback | Real target CPA and conditional kill/scale thresholds |
| Delivery capacity | Snapshot volume, response time and follow-up ownership | Safe Meta pacing and lead handling |

