## 6. Landing-page concept

Build one dedicated, navigation-reduced landing-page system on an approved ErgoWorks Consulting destination.

### Page principles

- **Launch default:** one dominant CTA on every baseline variant: request the free 15-minute Workplace Ergonomics Risk Snapshot—preliminary guidance only, **not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis**. Service-plan-primary variants are post-baseline tests only.
- Message-matched variants led by:

  1. Manual Handling Training
  2. Workstation and Ergonomic Assessment
  3. Hybrid and Home-office programmes

- Stripped header with ErgoWorks identity, an optional phone contact and no store or Physiotherapy navigation.
- Two-step form:

  1. business contact details;
  2. non-sensitive qualification fields such as team-size band, service need, location and timeframe.

- No injury history, symptoms, diagnoses, treatment, claim details or other health information.
- Separate required enquiry consent from optional, unchecked marketing consent.
- Clear explanation of what the Snapshot includes, what happens next and what it does not represent.
- Mobile-first performance, source/click-ID capture and a clear thank-you journey.
- Proof only after substantiation and written client approval.

The complete page architecture and copy are in [Appendix A](./appendices/A-landing-page-copy.md).

## 7. Measurement approach

Measurement is an upgrade to existing GA4-linked tracking—not a rebuild from zero.

### Conversion hierarchy

| Stage | Treatment |
|---|---|
| Valid Consulting enquiry | Primary initially |
| Qualified new-business Consulting call | Primary only when qualification rules can be enforced or reconciled |
| Valid B2B Snapshot request | Primary initially; preliminary guidance only—not a compliance assessment, compliance certification, medical assessment or diagnosis |
| CRM-qualified lead | Primary offline import once reliable |
| Proposal and closed-won | Downstream/value signals as volume and data quality permit |
| Newsletter, email click, click-to-call, call forwarding and local actions | Secondary |
| Physiotherapy actions | Excluded from Consulting campaign goals |

### Measurement stack

- Preserve Google auto-tagging and the existing GA4 link.
- Use campaign-specific Consulting conversion goals.
- Capture GCLID, GBRAID, WBRAID, FBCLID and UTMs in the CRM.
- Send qualified-lead, proposal and closed-won outcomes through Google Data Manager and Meta CAPI.
- Implement server-side GTM on a first-party domain such as `tags.ergoworksconsulting.com.au`.
- Use a Conversion Linker and Meta Pixel plus CAPI, preferably through CAPI Gateway.
- Use matching browser/server `event_id` values for deduplication.
- Use Data-Driven Attribution where eligible; do not use rule-based attribution.
- Implement **Consent Mode v2, default denied, with no client- or server-side analytics/advertising transmission before consent**, through an approved CMP.
- Enforce no pre-consent advertising or analytics transmissions unless Australian privacy/legal review explicitly approves a different configuration.
- Keep Consulting separate from Physiotherapy, ErgoEquip and Biosymm through dedicated or tightly scoped GA4 stream, Meta Dataset/Pixel, GTM triggers, audiences and CRM mappings.

### First-90-day measurement commitments

- 100% of approved Primary actions documented and tested.
- Newsletter and soft actions removed from Consulting bidding goals.
- Physiotherapy actions excluded from campaign 700072710 goals.
- CRM lead IDs and event IDs captured on valid lead records.
- Offline-event latency below 24 hours where operationally possible; 24–72 hours is a warning range.
- Meta lead-event EMQ of at least 8.0.
- Browser/server deduplication of at least 90%.
- Server/client hit ratio between 80% and 120%.
- At least six applicable Meta match parameters on eligible events.
- Weekly platform-to-CRM reconciliation.
- Zero sensitive-data events or parameters detected in testing.

The primary commercial KPI is **cost per qualified lead (CPQL)**. Raw CPL remains an entry-stage diagnostic. CAC and target CPQL cannot be set until contract value, contribution margin and stage-conversion rates are verified.

The full event taxonomy, consent requirements, field allowlist/deny list and QA plan are in [Appendix C](./appendices/C-tracking-spec.md).

### Methodology conflict

The generic ads-budget rubric recommends Maximize Clicks below 30 conversions per month. The live campaign, however, is mature, already uses Maximize Conversions and generates approximately 20 real leads per month while its current conversion signal is polluted.

Automatically switching to Maximize Clicks during measurement repair could optimise for traffic volume before query quality is understood. The account-specific recommendation is therefore to retain Maximize Conversions while cleaning and restabilising the baseline, then reassess:

| Clean post-remediation condition | Bidding decision |
|---|---|
| Fewer than 20 clean conversions/month with weak delivery and no qualified-lead imports | Consider a controlled Maximize Clicks test only after query review and with an evidence-based CPC cap |
| Approximately 20–29 clean conversions/month with stable query and lead quality | Retain Maximize Conversions and document the rubric variance |
| At least 30 clean conversions/month with stable CPA | Maximize Conversions is supported; assess tCPA readiness |
| More than 50 clean conversions/month with stable qualified-lead CPA | Consider tCPA |
| Reliable margin values and sufficient closed-won volume | Assess tROAS |

Do not use ECPC.

## 8. 30/60/90 roadmap

### Days 1–30 — Establish the foundation

