docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:38:No bidding or budget decision should precede conversion cleanup. Campaign 700072710 currently uses Maximize Conversions, so every primary action can influence bidding. Counting newsletter registrations and soft engagement actions as success risks directing spend toward users most likely to take easy actions rather than become qualified Consulting opportunities.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:69:2. Define a campaign-specific Consulting goal set for campaign 700072710.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:90:- Treat awards, client logos, Danone, “ASX 100” and “5.0/63 reviews” as **client sign-off required** before any paid-media use.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:96:Campaign 700072710 is verified as using **Maximize Conversions with no target CPA**. It produced 26 reported conversions in the last 30 days, but only approximately 20 appear to be real leads. The current optimisation signal is polluted by four Newsletter Sign Ups plus soft actions.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:136:Manual Handling Training consumed **A$2,069**, or **49% of the A$4,246 last-30-day spend**. This concentration is directionally plausible because “manual handling training” is the dominant verified demand term at approximately 2,700 Australian searches per month. Concentration alone is not proof of waste.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:163:Separately, the "DSA - Ergoworks Consulting" ad group spent **A$795 in the last 30 days (18.7% of spend, 55 clicks, 4.5 reported conversions)**. Conversion quality for that group total is unverified. The live keyword pull shows it is not a Dynamic Search Ads group: it holds nine static EXACT keywords—six competitor-keyword entries across four competitors plus three generics. Only the sampled government/competitor-query subset was near-zero converting. Its evidence gap is therefore not "DSA settings and final URLs" but whether the group-level 4.5 reported conversions represent qualified demand and whether the sampled leakage warrants tighter query controls (see Appendix B reclassification).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:181:The Brand ad group inside campaign 700072710 delivered **A$0 spend, zero clicks and zero conversions in the last 30 days**. Dedicated Brand routing and reporting are absent; service groups currently capture Brand queries.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:211:Campaign **16143562968 — Ergoworks Consulting PMax** is paused. The prescribed minimum for PMax is **A$50/day**, or **A$1,500 per 30-day planning month**.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:241:Campaign **843760968 — Ergoworks Consulting Remarketing** is paused. Remarketing can be rebuilt after consent and isolation requirements are satisfied; it should not simply be re-enabled in its current unknown configuration.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:292:| Negative keywords — **assessed, pending overblocking review** | Pulled: 419 campaign-level plus 74 ad-group-level negatives exist on 700072710 (full list in `research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`) | Review generic single-token broad negatives (e.g. "advice", "certification", "courses", "definition") that risk excluding legitimate MH-training queries, plus the accumulated single-first-name negatives | Overblocking and staleness review, not list construction from scratch |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:296:| Geography — **partial signal now available** | Search terms show a geo spread: "ergonomic office fyshwick" (Fyshwick = Canberra) A$250.00 / 18 clicks / 3 conv / 26% CTR is a strong-performing geo-specific term; terms also span sydney, canberra ×2, melbourne, brisbane and "near me" ×4, suggesting broad/national targeting against city-specific demand | Still required: user-location and matched-location performance reports (last 90 days and trailing 12 months) before city-level bid modifiers or a dedicated Canberra ad group — conditional on the clean-conversion baseline, since 3 conversions is not a stable base | Detect geographic waste and confirm “Presence” targeting |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:301:| Campaign settings | Full settings export for campaign 700072710 | Current; daily/shared budget, networks, locations, presence setting, schedule, language, URL options, search partners, Display expansion, audience mode and content exclusions | Identify structural leakage, budget starvation and inappropriate settings |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:306:| PMax | Full campaign 16143562968 export | Historical maximum available; asset groups, assets, search themes, audience signals, search categories, URL expansion, exclusions, negatives, brand exclusions and conversions | Validate park versus funded relaunch and identify cross-business contamination |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:307:| Remarketing | Full campaign 843760968 configuration and audience inventory | Current and historical; audience sources, membership duration, exclusions, placements, frequency and conversions | Determine whether to rebuild or retire the existing structure |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/E-existing-account-audit.md:311:| Proof permissions | Evidence and usage approval for testimonials, ratings, logos, awards, Danone and “ASX 100” | Current substantiation and written client approval | Determine which proof can legally and accurately appear in paid media |
