docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:240:| `GOOGLE_CONV_Consulting-AU_AU_2026Q3` | Existing non-brand Consulting demand capture; proposed renamed or labelled structure only after change-history review | Optimise existing campaign `700072710`; do not rebuild blindly |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:241:| Existing Brand ad group in campaign `700072710` | Dedicated Brand routing and reporting | Repair and consolidate in place first; consider a standalone campaign only after the observation gate below |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:247:Repair the existing Brand ad group in campaign `700072710`, verify its eligible RSA and Consulting destination, re-enable its three paused terms, and remove all confirmed service-group duplicates—`ergoworks` PHRASE, `ergoworks` EXACT and `ergoworks physio` PHRASE—from each of the five service ad groups. Then verify Brand query routing and separate Brand/service metrics for a full observation period. Consider a standalone Brand campaign only if Appendix E §E5's breakout conditions are met after that repair-in-place gate.
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:329:Canberra is not a Keyword Planner hypothesis: `ergonomic office canberra` (EXACT, QS=3) and `ergonomic office fyshwick` (PHRASE, ENABLED, QS=5) already exist as live keywords, and the fyshwick term produced **3 conversions from A$250.00 / 18 clicks at 26% CTR** in the last 30 days — observed converting inventory. Gate: Fyshwick is Canberra's furniture-retail district, so the query may carry equipment/showroom intent; pull the ad and conversion type behind that term before building on it, and treat any Canberra recommendation as conditional on the clean-conversion baseline (3 conversions is thin).
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:346:| Proof | Awards, Danone, logos, “ASX 100” and 5.0/63 reviews are **client sign-off required** before use |
docs/ergoworks-consulting/appendices/B-keyword-adgroup-sheets.md:350:A large negative inventory already exists: **419 campaign-level plus 74 ad-group-level negatives on campaign 700072710** (`research/live-keywords-negatives-2026-07-12.md`). The task is therefore not building a list from scratch but **auditing the existing 493 negatives** for overblocking, staleness (many single-name/person negatives suggest long accumulation) and gaps around the confirmed waste terms (certificate-intent and regulator queries from the 2026-07-12 search-terms pull).
